From 4624502010a6e289031aa650426240ec74d7bad0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lucascouts <lucascs@protonmail.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 03:49:07 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] feat(agent): refresh the account quota when the context ring
 is hovered

The 5-hour, weekly and model-scoped (Fable) rows 0011 and 0013 draw in the
context ring's tooltip only moved when the adapter decided to push them: at
session start, at the end of a turn, and on its idle poll. Hovering the ring
to read them showed whatever arrived last, and the tooltip itself was a
copy taken when it opened, so a number that arrived while it was open was
not shown until the next hover.

Two halves:

  * Active, on hover. Entering the ring calls
    `AcpThread::refresh_account_usage`, which sends `_claude/usage/refresh`
    (`{sessionId}` -> `{refreshed: bool}`) to an agent that advertises
    `agentCapabilities._meta["_claude/usage"].version >= 1`. The windows come
    back on the usual `usage_update` frames, so nothing on the receiving side
    changes. It is bounded twice: a request still in flight absorbs the next
    one, and a new one waits `ACCOUNT_USAGE_REFRESH_MIN_INTERVAL` (5 s) after
    the last was sent. An agent without the capability gets no request; the
    error is logged at debug level and the ring keeps what it has.

  * Live tooltip. `TokenUsageTooltip` observes the thread and rebuilds its
    quota rows when the thread changes, so the answer to the hover lands in
    front of the reader. The row building moved into `account_usage_rows`,
    shared by the ring and the tooltip.

The passive half -- every 30 s instead of 60 s -- lives in the adapter
(claude-agent-acp-plus, `QUOTA_POLL_DEFAULT_MS`), which already polls while
the session is idle and shares one sample across processes. The adapter
answers `refreshed: false` without asking the CLI while a turn runs: control
requests are served one at a time and a cancel waits behind them, and the
turn's own end refreshes the windows anyway.

Gating is on the capability, never on the entry id or the agent's name, as
for `_claude/tasks`; the peer harness of `acp_task_actions_tests.rs` gained
`connect_peer_with_meta` so a test can advertise any capability.

Tests: `refresh_account_usage_is_bounded_in_flight_and_in_time` (red with
either bound removed: 2 requests instead of 1, 4 instead of 2), and three in
`acp_usage_refresh_tests.rs` -- the request carries the session and
`refreshed` is read; `false` is an answer and a missing field an error; no
request without the capability, including for an agent that advertises
`_claude/tasks` only. acp_thread 341 passed, agent_servers 150 passed.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
